<?php
/**
 * Spartrak Footer.
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: node 561:9856 ("Footer Links", 1440x419). Verified byte-identical
 * across all three desktop frames that contain a footer — 561:9856 (checkout),
 * 595:14998 (home) and 704:24884 — same structure, padding, tokens, gaps,
 * column geometry and Arabic strings in every one. So there is one footer, not
 * a per-page variant.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * TWO REAL BUGS THIS REPLACES
 * ===========================================================================
 *  1. THE FOUR LINK COLUMNS RENDERED EMPTY. The previous template called
 *     `getChildHtml('spartrak.footer_links_1'..'_4')`, and those four blocks
 *     are declared NOWHERE in any layout XML in this theme — only
 *     `spartrak.footer_logo` exists. So every column emitted a title and then
 *     nothing. This is the exact failure the support strip already hit and
 *     documented (see support-strip.phtml's "CONTENT COMES FROM CODE, NOT CMS
 *     BLOCKS" note): child blocks that were never created, silently rendering
 *     empty on the live site.
 *
 *  2. THE STYLESHEET AND THE TEMPLATE DID NOT AGREE ON CLASS NAMES. _footer.less
 *     styled `__social-link`, `__contact`, `__contact-item`, `__support` and
 *     `__newsletter`; the template emitted `__social-links`,
 *     `__social-links-list`, `__social-links-item` and no contact markup at
 *     all. Every one of those rules was dead, which is why the social row had
 *     no 36px pill and the bottom bar had no phone/email at all.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * CONTENT COMES FROM CODE, NOT CMS BLOCKS
 * ===========================================================================
 * Same explicit project instruction the support strip records, and the same
 * three reasons apply verbatim here: it renders correctly on a fresh install
 * with zero admin setup (so the footer can never silently lose its links
 * again), the wording stays changeable WITHOUT a deploy because __() strings
 * are translatable per store view via Admin > Stores > Translations or this
 * theme's i18n/ar_EG.csv, and it keeps four static-block lookups off every
 * single page render (CLAUDE.md §4).
 *
 * The hotline reuses `__('Hotline')` and `__('12384')` — the SAME source
 * strings the support strip uses — so the header and footer can never show
 * different numbers. Note that Figma's footer draws 12304 while Figma's own
 * header draws 12384; rather than shipping both, one source wins and the
 * discrepancy is raised.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * RTL CHILD ORDER
 * ===========================================================================
 * These frames are RTL-composed, so child order here is the REVERSE of Figma's
 * LTR x-order — the convention header.phtml and support-strip.phtml already
 * establish and document. Concretely:
 *   - the brand block is emitted FIRST so RTL places it at the inline start
 *     (Figma x=1050, the right edge), and the four link columns follow in
 *     reverse so they land left-to-right as تواصل معنا / عن الشركة /
 *     خدمة العملاء / تسوق.
 *   - in the bottom bar, contact is emitted before copyright so copyright
 *     lands at the inline end (Figma x=0, the left).
 *   - inside each contact item the icon precedes the text, which puts the icon
 *     at the inline start — Figma's arrangement, and the conventional one in
 *     LTR too, so it needs no direction-specific override.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * LINK TARGETS — the one thing not derivable from Figma
 * ===========================================================================
 * Figma supplies the twenty labels but no hrefs. Every target below is
 * therefore a CONVENTIONAL Magento default collected into the single
 * `$href` map, so correcting one is a one-line change in one place rather
 * than a hunt through markup. `_direct` resolves to {base_url}/{identifier},
 * which is how a CMS page or category is linked by url key without a DB
 * lookup at render time.
 *
 * The four SOCIAL URLs are genuinely unknown business data — Figma provides no
 * hrefs and inventing an official brand account would be fabricating content.
 * They are left empty on purpose, and an empty entry renders the pill as a
 * non-interactive <span> instead of a dead <a href="#">: the Figma element is
 * still present and correctly styled, but nothing broken ships. Filling in
 * `$socialUrl` is all that is needed to activate them.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * FIGMA CONTENT ISSUES, reproduced verbatim and flagged rather than "fixed"
 * ===========================================================================
 *  - Column 1 ("تواصل معنا" / Contact us) lists فروعنا, الوظائف,
 *    سياسة الخصوصية and الشروط والاحكام — the same four items as column 2
 *    ("عن الشركة" / About the company). A Contact column carrying Privacy
 *    Policy and Careers reads like unfinished duplication in the source, but it
 *    is a content decision, not an orthographic slip, so it is reproduced
 *    exactly as drawn and raised for review.
 *  - The bottom-bar phone (+2012000000001, thirteen digits) and email
 *    (sparetrak@gmail.com) both look like placeholders. Reproduced as
 *    translatable literals, same mechanism as the hotline, so either can be
 *    corrected per store view without a deploy.
 *
 * @var \Smartwave\Porto\Block\Template $block
 */

/** Resolve a CMS page / category url key to an absolute storefront URL. */
$href = static function (string $identifier) use ($block): string {
    return $block->getUrl('', ['_direct' => $identifier]);
};

/**
 * The four link columns. Figma order is preserved in the DECLARATION (so this
 * reads the same way the design does, left to right); the reversal for RTL
 * happens once, at render, below.
 */
$columns = [
    [
        'title' => __('Contact Us'),
        // Rendered by $hotlineItem() rather than as a plain link: Figma gives
        // this one item mixed type — a regular muted label followed by a bold
        // ink number — which no other item in the footer has.
        'hotline' => true,
        'items' => [
            ['label' => __('Our branches'), 'url' => $href('branches')],
            ['label' => __('Careers'), 'url' => $href('careers')],
            ['label' => __('Privacy policy'), 'url' => $href('privacy-policy-cookie-restriction-mode')],
            ['label' => __('Terms and conditions'), 'url' => $href('terms-and-conditions')],
        ],
    ],
    [
        'title' => __('About'),
        'items' => [
            ['label' => __('About us'), 'url' => $href('about-us')],
            ['label' => __('Our branches'), 'url' => $href('branches')],
            ['label' => __('Careers'), 'url' => $href('careers')],
            ['label' => __('Privacy policy'), 'url' => $href('privacy-policy-cookie-restriction-mode')],
            ['label' => __('Terms and conditions'), 'url' => $href('terms-and-conditions')],
        ],
    ],
    [
        'title' => __('Customer Service'),
        'items' => [
            ['label' => __('Track your order'), 'url' => $block->getUrl('sales/guest/form')],
            ['label' => __('Return policy'), 'url' => $href('return-policy')],
            ['label' => __('Shipping policy'), 'url' => $href('shipping-policy')],
            ['label' => __('FAQ'), 'url' => $href('faq')],
            ['label' => __('Call us'), 'url' => $href('contact')],
        ],
    ],
    [
        'title' => __('Shop'),
        'items' => [
            ['label' => __('Engine parts'), 'url' => $href('engine-parts')],
            ['label' => __('Overhaul kit'), 'url' => $href('overhaul-kit')],
            ['label' => __('Pumps'), 'url' => $href('pumps')],
            ['label' => __('Filters'), 'url' => $href('filters')],
            ['label' => __('All brands'), 'url' => $href('brands')],
        ],
    ],
];

/**
 * Social channels, in Figma's left-to-right order. `url` is intentionally
 * empty — see the LINK TARGETS note above. Icons are the real 16x16 Figma
 * exports (561:9898 / 561:9901 / 561:9905 / 561:9910).
 */
$socialUrl = [
    'whatsapp' => '',
    'youtube' => '',
    'instagram' => '',
    'facebook' => '',
];

$social = [
    ['key' => 'whatsapp', 'label' => __('WhatsApp'), 'icon' => 'whatsapp.svg'],
    ['key' => 'youtube', 'label' => __('YouTube'), 'icon' => 'youtube.svg'],
    ['key' => 'instagram', 'label' => __('Instagram'), 'icon' => 'instagram.svg'],
    ['key' => 'facebook', 'label' => __('Facebook'), 'icon' => 'facebook.svg'],
];

/** Figma's mixed-type hotline row: muted label + bold ink number, 8px apart. */
$hotlineItem = static function () use ($block): string {
    $number = (string) __('12384');

    return '<li class="spartrak-footer__item">'
        . '<a class="spartrak-footer__link spartrak-footer__hotline" '
        . 'href="tel:' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($number) . '">'
        . '<span class="spartrak-footer__hotline-label">' . $block->escapeHtml(__('Hotline')) . '</span>'
        // Latin digits inside an Arabic run: isolate as LTR or the bidi
        // algorithm reorders them. Same fix as the support strip's own.
        . '<span class="spartrak-footer__hotline-number">' . $block->escapeHtml($number) . '</span>'
        . '</a>'
        . '</li>';
};

/**
 * One contact item in the bottom bar: 20x20 icon then text, 8px apart. The
 * value is a translatable literal so it is correctable per store view.
 */
$contactItem = static function (
    string $icon,
    string $value,
    string $scheme,
    string $label
) use ($block): string {
    return '<a class="spartrak-footer__contact-item" '
        . 'href="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($scheme . $value) . '" '
        . 'aria-label="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($label) . '">'
        . '<img class="spartrak-footer__contact-icon" '
        . 'src="' . $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/' . $icon)) . '" '
        . 'width="20" height="20" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />'
        . '<span class="spartrak-footer__contact-value">' . $block->escapeHtml($value) . '</span>'
        . '</a>';
};

$phone = (string) __('+2012000000001');
$email = (string) __('sparetrak@gmail.com');
?>
<footer class="spartrak-footer" role="contentinfo">
    <div class="spartrak-footer__links-area">
        <div class="spartrak-footer__row">
            <?php /* Emitted first so RTL puts it at the inline start (Figma x=1050). */ ?>
            <div class="spartrak-footer__brand">
                <div class="spartrak-footer__logo">
                    <?= $block->getChildHtml('spartrak.footer_logo') ?>
                </div>

                <p class="spartrak-footer__about">
                    <?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Al-Assal Trading and Supplies — over 50 years of experience supplying genuine diesel engine spare parts for every global brand. Mohsen Al-Assal and Partners.')) ?>
                </p>

                <ul class="spartrak-footer__social">
                    <?php foreach (array_reverse($social) as $channel): ?>
                        <?php
                        $url = $socialUrl[$channel['key']] ?? '';
                        $iconHtml = '<img src="'
                            . $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/' . $channel['icon']))
                            . '" width="16" height="16" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />';
                        ?>
                        <li class="spartrak-footer__social-item">
                            <?php if ($url !== ''): ?>
                                <a class="spartrak-footer__social-link"
                                   href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($url) ?>"
                                   rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
                                   aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($channel['label']) ?>">
                                    <?= /* @noEscape */ $iconHtml ?>
                                </a>
                            <?php else: ?>
                                <?php /* No URL supplied — see the LINK TARGETS note. Rendered as
                                        the same styled pill, but inert, so no dead href ships. */ ?>
                                <span class="spartrak-footer__social-link"
                                      role="img"
                                      aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($channel['label']) ?>">
                                    <?= /* @noEscape */ $iconHtml ?>
                                </span>
                            <?php endif; ?>
                        </li>
                    <?php endforeach; ?>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <?php /* Reversed for RTL — see the RTL CHILD ORDER note. */ ?>
            <?php foreach (array_reverse($columns) as $index => $column): ?>
                <?php $titleId = 'spartrak-footer-col-' . $index; ?>
                <nav class="spartrak-footer__col" aria-labelledby="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($titleId) ?>">
                    <h2 class="spartrak-footer__col-title" id="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($titleId) ?>">
                        <?= $block->escapeHtml($column['title']) ?>
                    </h2>
                    <ul class="spartrak-footer__list">
                        <?php if (!empty($column['hotline'])): ?>
                            <?= /* @noEscape */ $hotlineItem() ?>
                        <?php endif; ?>
                        <?php foreach ($column['items'] as $item): ?>
                            <li class="spartrak-footer__item">
                                <a class="spartrak-footer__link" href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($item['url']) ?>">
                                    <?= $block->escapeHtml($item['label']) ?>
                                </a>
                            </li>
                        <?php endforeach; ?>
                    </ul>
                </nav>
            <?php endforeach; ?>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spartrak-footer__bottom">
        <div class="spartrak-footer__bottom-row">
            <?php /* Contact first so copyright lands at the inline end (Figma x=0). */ ?>
            <?php /* Email before phone, so RTL lands phone at the inline end —
                     Figma puts the phone group LEFT of the email group (phone at
                     x=0, email at x=203 inside the 427 contact frame), confirmed
                     against the node's own 1440 PNG export. Same reversal rule as
                     everywhere else in this template. */ ?>
            <div class="spartrak-footer__contact">
                <?= /* @noEscape */ $contactItem('email.svg', $email, 'mailto:', (string) __('Email us')) ?>
                <?= /* @noEscape */ $contactItem('phone.svg', $phone, 'tel:', (string) __('Call us')) ?>
            </div>

            <p class="spartrak-footer__copyright">
                <?= $block->escapeHtml(__('© %1 - All rights reserved to SpareTrak', date('Y'))) ?>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>
